From: harshanandak <harshanandak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 13:21:33 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] docs: four more claims corrected against the actual repo
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- validate.md said the lefthook gates run "the same jobs CI runs". ci.yml runs
  build, test, lint and type-check but never sync:agents --check, so a commit
  that skips the local hooks, or lands via the web UI or automation, can carry
  stale generated harness files. Say which gate is local-only and why.
- verify.md's rules called the command read-only. Its own Steps 6-8 remove a
  worktree, force-delete a branch, and open/close beads issues. It never
  touches history, but it is not observation-only — enumerate the mutations.
- premerge.md still routed convention updates into a CLAUDE.md USER block.
  CLAUDE.md is a 12-byte @AGENTS.md pointer with no markers; the step could
  not be followed and risked overwriting the pointer. Points at AGENTS.md now.
- forge-workflow.md's index linked docs/TOOLCHAIN.md and docs/VALIDATION.md,
  neither of which exists, and called itself AGENTS.md. Both dead links
  removed and the file's actual role as a sync source stated.

Found by codex review on PR #132.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
